WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.520
- We'll let's start with
my first guest now,

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.520
she's a actress and
director and you know her

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.730
from that 70s show on
"Orange is the new Black"

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.477
now she has a new bestselling book called

00:00:07.477 --> 00:00:10.560
"You and I as Mothers A Raw
and Honest Guide to Motherhood"

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:12.340
It's Laura Prepon.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.537
- Hi
- Hi

00:00:13.537 --> 00:00:15.360
(laughing)

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.730
Oh my Gosh, hello I'm such a big fan.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.870
You're so talented.
- Oh my God, you too,

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.210
Thank you so much for having me on.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.670
- No, thank you, I saw your,
I just don't ever see pictures

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.030
I'm never in the limelight ever

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:29.670
and I just see you in
my head as a redhead.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.057
So I'm like seeing and I was like,

00:00:31.057 --> 00:00:33.420
"I know Lauren Prepon
but this is not her."

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.290
And I was like, you're
like such a different human

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:37.560
with dark hair, it's beautiful.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.530
- So thank you, it's so weird, I mean,

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:42.070
I did this because for
"Orange is the New Black"

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:44.340
- Yeah
- And then when we--

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.150
I was pregnant when we wrapped

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.590
and then I couldn't change my hair color.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.400
And then I just gave
birth a few months ago

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.900
and now it's a pandemic and now
I can't get my hair changed.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.490
- Here in my, I know my roots
so I'm just like whatever.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:57.740
So how is it going though?

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:59.150
Speaking of "Orange is the New Black"

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:01.380
was that any kind of
prep for quarantine time?

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.330
Coz you know we are stuck in one place.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:08.360
- Yeah, I mean, honestly we...

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:11.500
I mean, look, I was
already pretty prepared,

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:14.830
just with the whole that my
baby was coming and everything,

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:18.110
we were already planning
on isolating and yeah,

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:21.380
I mean I don't know if "Orange"
really prepared me but,

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.030
- Yeah
- is that you know,

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:25.830
there are so many of us
together all the time

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:30.270
but in terms of you know, the
fact that I just had a baby

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.300
that really prepared you know,

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.390
the fact that we were already
planning on isolating,

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:38.403
definitely I think made the
transition a little smoother.

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:42.470
We try to laugh when we
can, it's hard Kelly.

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:43.520
- Oh my gosh, you know

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.860
humor has gotten me through many times.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:47.460
So I'm with you with that.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.470
But I hear that you're
to get you through times,

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:51.640
we have something in common you love games

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:53.080
like you're competitive.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:54.990
Do you play poker?

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.201
Did I hear right that you play poker?

00:01:57.201 --> 00:01:59.590
- That was another life but yes.

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:01.140
- Oh, it's the time when you were cool

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:02.810
and had a life before kids and everything?

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:03.643
(laughing)

00:02:03.643 --> 00:02:04.476
I always say that I'm like,

00:02:04.476 --> 00:02:06.449
"Oh it was not as cool and I did things."

00:02:06.449 --> 00:02:07.282
(laughter)

00:02:07.282 --> 00:02:08.650
- I used to play so much.

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:10.730
I mean, I played in
the World Series twice.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.160
I was on the cover
- That's crazy!

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:16.680
- No, I was I was obsessed. I actually,

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:19.479
I was on the cover of a poker magazine.

00:02:19.479 --> 00:02:20.373
- Wow, yeah!
- I was playing

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:22.570
like I was totally--

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:23.420
- But you're an actor, though.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.400
So you're really good at bluffing so

00:02:26.405 --> 00:02:28.040
- I did pretty well.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.180
I was really into it.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:31.220
But now with kids,

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:33.200
I don't have time to
go sit at a card table.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.710
- Oh my gosh, no, I feel you.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:36.087
Her new book y'all is called

00:02:36.087 --> 00:02:39.270
"You and I as Mothers a Raw and
Honest Guide to Motherhood."

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:41.850
I feel like there's so
many books out there

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.340
and so many guides for

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:46.150
but there's not many,
like I love your title.

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:48.520
And I know the vibe of it
being like raw and real

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.890
and like the ups and downs of everything.

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:55.300
I feel like everything doesn't
prepare you for all of that.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.410
So what made you want to open up

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:58.460
the way you did in your new book

00:02:58.460 --> 00:02:59.540
'cause you're very honest

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:02.070
about things that maybe people
would never tell people.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.010
- Yeah, I honestly for me

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:06.770
I felt like there were all
these books about pregnancy

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:08.810
and there were all these books, you know,

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:11.550
leading you up to when
you become a mother,

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:15.610
but I didn't find any resources for me

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:16.950
once I became a mother.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:20.403
And I was like, what about
the rest of my life, you know?

00:03:21.354 --> 00:03:23.450
So for me I felt like

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:25.980
there really wasn't
anything out there for us

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:28.020
and there wasn't a resource for me.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:29.853
So I wrote the book I was looking for you,

00:03:29.853 --> 00:03:32.240
I interviewed a bunch of women in it

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:35.130
to speak to all these common themes

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:38.170
so the reader can find
someone to relate to

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:40.850
'cause we all go through similar things,

00:03:40.850 --> 00:03:43.840
even if we are in our
different stages of motherhood

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:46.020
it's not this isn't a postpartum book

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:47.950
it's for mothers of all ages, yeah.

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:50.620
- No, I love that it's really honest.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:52.670
I think that that's important
I also think it's important

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:54.920
that you're just writing just being a mom,

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:58.920
especially a young mom of young kids, like

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:02.140
it's really important you
have some sort of mom squad,

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:05.190
like you have some like,
or even a friend squad,

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:07.730
they don't have to be all moms
but just to understand like

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:10.360
where you're coming from
and to have that kind of,

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:12.700
I don't know that bond,
like, can you talk about that

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:14.650
in the book about moms squads, right?

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:17.550
- Yeah. I mean, I, you know,
just like you said, like

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:20.250
it's just really important especially now

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.550
with all of the quarantine
and self-isolation.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:24.760
I mean, people are starting
to go back out again,

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:27.460
but nothing like we did of course.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:32.190
And with social distancing, I
find that already being a mom

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:35.770
can feel isolating and you know,

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:38.010
especially now with
everything we're going through

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:40.130
with the pandemic it's
even more isolating.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:44.240
So anything you can do to
help build that community,

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:45.230
is so important.

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:47.040
And I write about that
because that's something

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.520
I really had to learn.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:50.810
But now as a mother,

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:53.560
I do feel like it's really
important to have that,

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.410
whether whoever that is for you,

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:57.900
whoever your community is for you.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.310
- So what advice, like what kind of advice

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:02.230
has your mom's squad
given you like personally,

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:04.040
like you've kind of I struggled with.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:07.330
- Well, when I had my,
for, you know, my baby,

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:09.670
I just had a boy, but
when I had my daughter,

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:11.560
who's now about two and a half,

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:14.020
I went back to work at six weeks

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:17.070
and I was directing by the
time she was four months old.

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:22.070
And I remember, talking to
Mila about being a working mom

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:26.930
and she gave me a really cool
piece of advice, which was

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:29.960
when you talk to your kids,
like about going to work,

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:33.530
she's never like, "Oh, that
sucks, mommy has to go to work."

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:35.860
She always puts a really
positive spin on it

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:36.837
and she's always like,

00:05:36.837 --> 00:05:38.920
"Mommy has to go to work.
Isn't that awesome?"

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:40.790
Like she puts a really
positive thing on it

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:45.320
so that her children associate
positivity with work.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:48.130
And that's something I
thought was really cool,

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:49.760
especially cause I was struggling so much

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:52.610
with going back to work so quickly.

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:54.830
And you know, another example

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:57.520
that kind of feeds into
the mom, guilt of it all

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:59.313
is quality over quantity.

00:06:00.260 --> 00:06:03.140
One of my friends, Amber
Tamblyn shared that with me,

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:05.550
'cause her daughter's a
little older than mine

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:08.070
and you can be with your family,

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:11.540
but if you're on your
phone or fielding emails or

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:13.440
- you're not present
- on social media,

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:14.920
whatever you're doing, you're not present.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:15.780
You're not even there.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:16.830
So it's like

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:19.460
quality over quantity when
you're with your family,

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:23.000
you make it really quality
time and really be present

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.830
and are there that's something
that really helped me too,

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:27.100
it's just when I am with my family,

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:28.210
having very quality time,

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:32.100
don't try to work while
I'm with my family.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:35.973
That's something that has
really helped me a lot, so

00:06:35.973 --> 00:06:37.780
- Yeah.
- That's great.

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:39.560
- So you opened up in the book about

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:41.160
like speaking of being
personal from the beginning,

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:43.970
that's what I loved about
how raw and real you are.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:44.890
'Cause I feel like sometimes

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:48.040
that's few and far between
with people and the public eye.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.430
But you had to make an impossible decision

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:51.671
during a pregnancy.

00:06:51.671 --> 00:06:55.100
And I have known people that
have had the same scenario.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.790
So what happened with this situation?

00:06:57.790 --> 00:06:58.910
How did you cope with it?

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:01.690
'Cause it's a, that's a
big thing to open up about.

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:02.890
- Well, what's interesting is that

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:05.750
when I first we had to make a decision

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:09.210
because we found out once we
got into the second trimester,

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:11.500
by the way, but it's usually, you know,

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:13.710
once you get into that,
you're like "I'm in the clear"

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:14.830
- Yeah
- But we found out

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:17.830
when we were into our second
trimester, that there were,

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:20.830
some pretty devastating health problems.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:24.100
And that the baby was
at risk I was at risk,

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:25.570
the baby probably wouldn't survive

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:28.340
and then I was at risk
for carrying any longer.

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:30.840
And we really weren't in a position to...

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:33.683
the writing was on the wall
there was nothing we could do.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:37.330
And it might, my husband and I often say

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:42.330
that was the worst day of our
lives, making that decision

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:46.710
and it's once I went through it,

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:49.890
I was really mad at my body and myself

00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:51.530
like I thought I did
something to cause it,

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:52.573
which I didn't,

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:57.840
but you just are trying
so hard to find an answer.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:00.370
And I found that once I went through that,

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:02.130
I started finding out
about these other women

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:04.770
who've gone through similar losses

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:06.890
and nobody was talking about it,

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:07.960
- Yeah
- but I felt that

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:10.260
it was really important to write about it

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:14.120
because I wanted other people
to be able to feel safe,

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:15.850
to share their story.

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:18.160
And the fact that I wrote about it,

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:21.220
I can't tell you how many
people have reached out.

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:22.130
- I can't imagine
- explaining

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:25.270
how much it's helped them
and now they're able to

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:28.990
vocalize what they went through
or they feel seen and heard

00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:32.730
and it's something that was
really hard for me to share,

00:08:32.730 --> 00:08:36.900
but I'm so glad I did, because
it really helped again,

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:38.000
built this community

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.600
and made it safer for
people to talk about.

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:43.430
- Yeah, and I mean, I'm
one who loves therapy,

00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:45.580
so I just sometimes like
learning and they were like,

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:48.610
just saying it aloud helps you heal,

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:51.190
like just saying it out loud
and not keeping it inside,

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:53.360
and it just kinda building up like

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:55.430
saying it aloud helps the person saying it

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.390
just as much as somebody
connecting to the message

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:58.280
and feeling the same way.

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:00.450
So it's very brave and it's very cool

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:02.930
and you're very strong woman.

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:03.930
- Thank you.
- All right, well

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:05.040
thank you so much

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:06.587
and Laura's book everybody

00:09:06.587 --> 00:09:09.980
"You and I as mothers A Raw
and Honest Guide to Motherhood"

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:10.890
is available now.

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:12.160
Go and get it I promise

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:14.090
all you mamas out there are mamas-to-be.

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:15.887
It's a good one. Go find that one.

